<commerce>
What a commerce hook is:
- strategy.commerceHooks[] contains reusable conversion angles (feature→benefit + objection + CTA style).
- In the outline, you do NOT rewrite the hook. You reference it by id using section.commerceHookIds[].

Where hooks are allowed:
- ONLY add commerceHookIds to sections that include featuredAssetIds (i.e., product is actually featured).
- Do NOT add commerce hooks to sections with no featuredAssetIds.

Coverage rule:
- Every strategy.commerceHooks[].id MUST appear at least once across the outline’s sections.commerceHookIds[].

How to add hooks:
- Use edits with op="push" to add hook ids into section.commerceHookIds[].
- Prefer 1 hook per eligible section; use 2 only if the section must cover two different objections.

Example:
strategy.commerceHooks = [
  { "id": "hook_eye_trust", ... },
  { "id": "hook_moist_fit", ... }
]

Correct edits:
{
  "edits": [
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.2.commerceHookIds", "value": "hook_eye_trust" },
    { "op": "push", "path": "sections.7.commerceHookIds", "value": "hook_moist_fit" }
  ]
}

Incorrect:
- adding commerceHookIds to a section that has no featuredAssetIds
- inventing hook ids not present in strategy.commerceHooks
- replacing commerceHookIds instead of pushing
</commerce>
